  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the following four compounds I, II, III, and IV.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/a71981bc-6caa-48dc-be6d-78323bed3ecc-image.png\"/></p><p>Choose the correct statement(s).</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "JXbWd",
      "text": "The order of basicity is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>IV</mi></math>.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "y5uDX",
      "text": "The magnitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math> difference between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;is more than that between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IV</mi></math>.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "PMUEp",
      "text": "Resonance effect is more in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math> than in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IV</mi></math>.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lfDC4",
      "text": "Steric effect makes compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IV</mi></math> more basic than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math>.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The correct basic strength order is</p><p>(A)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#8739;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>;</mo></math></p><ul>\t<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IV</mi></math> is strongest base due to SIR effect.</li>\t<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math> is weakest base due to<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> group of three nitro groups present at Ortho and Para positions.</li>\t<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Il</mi></math> is stronger than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math> is tertiary and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> primary aromatic amine.</li></ul><p>(B)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IV</mi></math> is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>000</mn></math>&nbsp;times more basic than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math>. While <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> differ very little in basic strength.</p><p>(C,D) Due to SIR effect in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IV</mi></math> both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math> will be out of plane hence resonance effect is more in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math>&nbsp;than in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IV</mi></math>.<br />in III than in $\\mathrm{V}$.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
